│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The core issue is that Sphinx is encountering references to        │
│ genindex, modindex, and search within the toctree directive, but   │
│ these are not actually defined or generated. This likely stems     │
│ from a configuration issue within Sphinx, potentially related to   │
│ how the index extensions are being used. The StackOverflow links   │
│ suggest custom index generation might be involved, but without     │
│ access to the full codebase, it’s difficult to pinpoint the exact  │
│ cause. A simple fix is to remove the references to these           │
│ non-existent indices from the toctree directive. This will prevent │
│ the warning from appearing, although it won't actually generate    │
│ the indices.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
